  RowBox[{"displacement", " ", "->", " ", "extendedHoppingMatrix"}]], 
  "InlineCode",
  ScriptLevel->0,
  ShowStringCharacters->True,
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontWeight->"Plain",
  FontSlant->"Plain",ExpressionUUID->"ec3321fc-5f97-4646-9c3a-cdfdf2191eb3"],
 ", or the two-list layered scattering-region block representation. Every \
matrix uses internal-major, photon-minor ordering with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TagBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", " ", "m"}], "+", "1"}],
    HoldForm], TraditionalForm]], "InlineMath",
  ScriptLevel->0,
  FractionBoxOptions->{BaseStyle->{ScriptLevel -> 0}},ExpressionUUID->
  "1ab2f164-523f-1f47-9475-9e5a6bbd1434"],
 " photon sectors."
}], "Notes",
 CellID->598331088,ExpressionUUID->"60929911-eee5-aa4b-81c4-27e3bb742c03"],

Cell["\<\
For displacement associations, block multiplication adds displacement \
vectors. Supply a complete directed-hopping association when needed to \
represent a Hermitian model.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->176640995,ExpressionUUID->"65f0e215-d20a-9042-aff4-7abbc09a4912"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For scattering-region input, block multiplication contracts layer indices. \
If the effective result contains nonzero couplings between nonadjacent \
layers, the implementation emits a message and returns ",
 Cell[BoxData["$Failed"], "InlineCode",
  ScriptLevel->0,
  ShowStringCharacters->True,
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontWeight->"Plain",
  FontSlant->"Plain",ExpressionUUID->"93e6616c-d8a0-8542-8ac8-53cc9168a953"],
 " because the two-list form cannot represent them."
}], "Notes",
 CellID->1930432700,ExpressionUUID->"ceb98c6a-a20f-2348-8afd-098e241564eb"],

